News fragments
--------------

Each change that belongs in NEWS gets its own file in this directory.  At
release time, towncrier collects the files into NEWS and removes them.

Name the file <bug>.<type>, e.g. 984255.bugfix, or +<name>.<type> for a
change without a bug, e.g. +estrip-prefix.bugfix.  The types are:

  summary      Paragraphs below the release heading
  breaking     Breaking changes
  security     Security
  feature      Features
  bugfix       Bug fixes
  performance  Performance
  cleanup      Cleanups

The file contains the entry as it should appear in NEWS, without the
leading "* " and the indentation.  Separate further paragraphs with a
blank line:

  vartree: Skip preserve-libs linkmap rebuild when it is unnecessary.

  This improves merge time performance.

For a file named after a bug, "(bug #N)" is added to the end of the first
paragraph.  If a change fixes several bugs, symlink the other bug numbers
to the first fragment:

  ln -s 175808.feature NEWS.d/222601.feature

A second fragment for the same bug and type takes a counter, e.g.,
984255.bugfix.1.

Entries are sorted by their text.  Starting an entry with the component,
as in commit messages, keeps related changes together.

Cheat sheet
-----------

  towncrier create --edit 984255.bugfix       # new fragment
  towncrier create --edit +<name>.feature     # new fragment without a bug
  towncrier build --draft --version 3.0.85    # preview the next release
  towncrier build --yes --version 3.0.85      # update NEWS, git rm fragments

Always pass --version.  Without it, towncrier uses the version of the
installed portage.
